Watashi ga sanka suru

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:20.086
Hisabisa no doraibu de minna hai tenshon

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:22.350
Hisabisa no doraibu de minna hai tenshon

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:25.220
Kare mo kuru no

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:28.822
Myaku ga ima wa nakutomo

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:32.563
Zettai ikimasu tomo

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:38.603
Sugoi sugoi pookaa faisu dato shitara

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:41.741
Aru yo nante

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:45.812
Umi wa hiyake suru kara, yama ni shiyou tte

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:48.781
Umi wa hiyake suru kara, yama ni shiyou tte

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:53.920
Koo-to no kisetsu nanoni kanchigai shiteru

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:58.357
Koo-to no kisetsu nanoni kanchigai shiteru

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:02.595
Doushite nano?

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:06.566
Konna ureshikute

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:14.371
Chigiresouna hodo waratte iru noni

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:22.916
Kare no senaka mite wa mune tsumaru

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:30.880
Taenai egao no utsu no naka de

00:01:37.464 --> 00:01:39.091
Are you really going to summon them?

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:40.995
How many times do I have to say it?

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:43.570
Those girls are going to be crushed, you know.

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:45.338
Are you suggesting that I should
give them special treatment?

00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:46.573
That's not what I was implying.

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:48.208
So what were you implying?

00:01:48.208 --> 00:01:51.803
I feel like those girls have potential.

00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:53.546
Based on what, may I ask?

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:55.241
It's just a hunch.

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:58.480
You should listen to yourself.

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:01.020
Your hunches aren't always on
though, are they?

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.021
Historically speaking.

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:03.656
What are you talking about?

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:05.258
If they are crushed,

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:07.590
that just means they never had
potential to begin with, doesn't it?

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:10.759
You're cold as always.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:14.400
Episode #4
Where Are We Going?

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.803
Episode #4
Where Are We Going?
Four are absent and one was late.

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:17.003
Episode #4
Where Are We Going?

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:17.704
Episode #4
Where Are We Going?
Really?

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:20.140
Episode #4
Where Are We Going?
There are also some cases of graffiti
of the bulletin board.

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:20.540
There are also some cases of graffiti
of the bulletin board.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.208
I'll look into that later.

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:24.010
Thanks, I appreciate it.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:25.375
You're welcome!

00:02:28.882 --> 00:02:30.372
Good morning!

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:33.286
You're fifteen minutes late.

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:34.254
Sorry...

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:37.155
I'd appreciate it if you'd remember
that you're a member of Grace.

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:39.859
Paula?

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:41.190
Go to class.

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:43.395
I'll talk to Kate.

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:45.955
Um, but...

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:47.329
Now.

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:50.562
Okay...

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:06.350
Are you all right?

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:08.681
Yes, I'm sorry.

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:12.924
Recently, it doesn't seem like you're all right.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:18.788
Shouldn't you have been lined up with the
members of Grace at Lise's funeral?

00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:21.064
It was hard...

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:25.638
to see Lise from where you were standing.

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:31.235
But we're members of Grace.
We represent our school.

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:33.313
I know...

00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:35.372
I'm going to overlook your tardiness today.

00:03:36.149 --> 00:03:39.641
I know that you and Lise had
a special friendship.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:42.211
This has been hard for me too.

00:03:42.322 --> 00:03:43.914
Again, I'm sorry.

00:03:45.625 --> 00:03:47.393
I'll get to class.

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:48.690
Wait!

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.723
I hate to have to tell you this, but...

00:03:52.131 --> 00:03:56.329
There's a detective here today.
He wants to talk to you.

00:03:57.704 --> 00:04:00.502
Everyone says that you were close to her.

00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:02.697
Is that so?

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:05.042
Shall I go with you to talk to him?

00:04:06.946 --> 00:04:08.573
It's no problem.

00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:10.973
I'll be fine by myself.

00:04:12.018 --> 00:04:13.315
Really?

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:17.585
If you need anything,
come and talk to me, okay?

00:04:19.092 --> 00:04:20.719
Thank you.

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:44.784
At this school,

00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:47.412
all the kids wearing uniforms are members of
some sort of student group, correct?

00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:50.351
Yes, that's right.

00:04:50.857 --> 00:04:53.087
And this group is called "Grace," right?

00:04:53.359 --> 00:04:54.527
Yes...

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:57.664
And you're regarded as the creme de la creme

00:04:57.664 --> 00:04:59.427
even from within the school, I'd imagine.

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:01.824
I don't really know.

00:05:02.302 --> 00:05:06.398
Of course, it's hard to say so
when you're one of them.

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:11.501
But thanks to Grace, this school
seems to run like clockwork.

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:12.845
Right?

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:14.013
Yeah...

00:05:14.013 --> 00:05:15.913
All serious students...

00:05:16.649 --> 00:05:20.278
Today, we're here to talk to
some people about Lise.

00:05:20.887 --> 00:05:21.954
I see.

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:25.151
I hear that you were particularly close to her.

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:30.394
Yes, but recently, the only time I'd see her
was in class every now and then.

00:05:31.764 --> 00:05:33.199
Why was that?

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:34.901
Were you having a disagreement or something?

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:38.004
No, it's just that recently I was chosen
to be a member of Grace

00:05:38.004 --> 00:05:40.404
and since then, I've been busy
with those activities.

00:05:41.407 --> 00:05:42.840
I see.

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:47.240
So recently, you hadn't been having lunch
or hanging out together much?

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:48.715
That's right.

00:05:48.715 --> 00:05:51.377
Well, in that case this may
be hard to answer, but...

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:55.176
Had you noticed anything out of
the ordinary with her?

00:05:55.388 --> 00:05:57.256
Such as acting strange or anything?

00:05:57.256 --> 00:05:58.791
Or her taste in clothing changing,

00:05:58.791 --> 00:05:59.815
or she found a new boyfriend?

00:06:00.026 --> 00:06:02.392
Things like that. Anything is fine.
Did you notice anything?

00:06:03.763 --> 00:06:06.332
Nothing in particular.

00:06:06.332 --> 00:06:07.822
I see...

00:06:08.835 --> 00:06:11.337
When did you last see Lise?

00:06:11.337 --> 00:06:15.273
The day before she went missing.
I think we had a class together.

00:06:15.341 --> 00:06:16.876
And what did you talk about that day?

00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:18.673
Well, nothing really.

00:06:18.978 --> 00:06:20.445
I see...

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:23.844
Well, thanks. Sorry to bother you
at a time like this.

00:06:26.419 --> 00:06:31.584
Ultimately, we haven't heard anything that would
suggest this was a suicide, have we?

00:06:32.091 --> 00:06:33.718
That's true...

00:06:34.494 --> 00:06:36.562
A regular, happy student committing
suicide all of a sudden,

00:06:36.562 --> 00:06:39.122
having given no signs whatsoever...

00:06:39.499 --> 00:06:42.093
It's just like all the other cases, you know.

00:06:42.735 --> 00:06:45.260
Yeah, something about them
just doesn't feel right.

00:06:45.938 --> 00:06:47.769
Do we keep going?

00:06:49.575 --> 00:06:50.643
You know...

00:06:50.643 --> 00:06:51.644
What?

00:06:51.644 --> 00:06:53.679
That girl from the students'
club we just talked to...

00:06:53.679 --> 00:06:55.408
You mean Kate Ashley from Grace?

00:06:55.648 --> 00:06:57.081
That girl...

00:06:57.683 --> 00:06:59.651
It seemed like there's something
she's not telling us.

00:07:00.653 --> 00:07:01.984
That girl?

00:07:02.588 --> 00:07:04.317
It's just a feeling...

00:07:06.626 --> 00:07:08.253
Grace, huh?

00:07:08.661 --> 00:07:10.288
This is one strange island.

00:07:13.232 --> 00:07:15.496
My house is crazy in the morning.

00:07:16.235 --> 00:07:19.534
I have to chase down my little
brother and sister.

00:07:19.739 --> 00:07:21.908
Make them eat their breakfasts; get
them out of their pajamas;

00:07:21.908 --> 00:07:23.398
then get them dressed and
ready to go to daycare;

00:07:23.743 --> 00:07:25.836
and finally take them to the bus stop.

00:07:26.212 --> 00:07:27.679
That sounds like a chore.

00:07:28.214 --> 00:07:31.809
But I like being busy.

00:07:32.452 --> 00:07:34.545
If I'm not, I start thinking about that.

00:07:35.021 --> 00:07:36.488
I know...

00:07:36.823 --> 00:07:38.916
I wonder how Rachel and Claire are?

00:07:39.826 --> 00:07:41.487
I don't think they've been comng to school.

00:07:48.801 --> 00:07:53.204
I wonder if Claire and Rachel think
about all this when they're alone?

00:07:55.174 --> 00:07:57.665
A bunch of strange thoughts...

00:07:59.212 --> 00:08:01.510
All this is a heavy burden to bear alone.

00:08:04.283 --> 00:08:07.013
Hey, wanna leave school together early today?

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:08.120
What?

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:08.754
Let's go see how those two are doing.
What?

00:08:08.754 --> 00:08:09.846
Let's go see how those two are doing.

00:08:10.456 --> 00:08:11.753
Kate?

00:08:19.565 --> 00:08:21.260
I wouldn't have expected...

00:08:22.134 --> 00:08:25.069
that you'd worry about those two like that.

00:08:25.671 --> 00:08:27.273
Because I'm in Grace?

00:08:27.273 --> 00:08:31.539
Huh? No, that's not why, I...

00:08:31.611 --> 00:08:33.078
I understand.

00:08:34.514 --> 00:08:38.751
Sara's my only friend whose house I've been to.

00:08:38.751 --> 00:08:39.752
Really?

00:08:39.752 --> 00:08:41.454
And I've only been there twice.

00:08:41.454 --> 00:08:44.590
I've just been too busy since my mom
checked in to the hospital.

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:49.357
I just don't have time to do things like go to
friends' houses or go shopping with them.

00:08:49.929 --> 00:08:53.888
But I don't know, cutting school like this...

00:08:55.868 --> 00:08:58.393
It's...I just think it's crazy.

00:08:59.572 --> 00:09:01.274
Why do you think that?

00:09:01.274 --> 00:09:04.209
Well, it's just hard to do something like that.

00:09:05.077 --> 00:09:07.102
But it's not like we were screwing around.

00:09:08.114 --> 00:09:11.015
Everything has been such a shock.

00:09:11.551 --> 00:09:14.577
And I suppose doing something like
this from time to time...

00:09:15.621 --> 00:09:18.224
would be fun and help me forget
about things for a while.

00:09:18.224 --> 00:09:22.160
Me too. Thinking about it is
more than I can handle.

00:09:24.363 --> 00:09:25.921
This is good for me too.

00:09:26.832 --> 00:09:30.036
Hanging out like this really puts me at ease.

00:09:30.036 --> 00:09:31.003
Really?

00:09:36.642 --> 00:09:40.580
That's why I'm saying, I don't feel well.

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:44.083
In the past, you'd at least text me and
let me know you weren't coming.

00:09:44.083 --> 00:09:47.849
Okay, I'm sorry. It's just that
I've been sleeping.

00:09:48.621 --> 00:09:51.920
What's up with you?
You've been acting weird lately.

00:09:52.825 --> 00:09:55.453
I think it's that I've had a cold for a while now.

00:09:55.861 --> 00:09:57.488
So you don't think you can make it tonight?

00:09:59.699 --> 00:10:00.996
Rachel...

00:10:01.233 --> 00:10:03.436
Well, maybe I'll go.

00:10:03.436 --> 00:10:04.733
Really?!

00:10:04.971 --> 00:10:05.838
Maybe it'll make me feel better.

00:10:05.838 --> 00:10:07.499
Yeah, we'll just chill.
Maybe it'll make me feel better.

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:09.107
Yeah...

00:10:09.475 --> 00:10:10.772
Oh, hang on a second.

00:10:11.510 --> 00:10:12.778
Yes?

00:10:12.778 --> 00:10:14.439
Your friends are here.

00:10:14.914 --> 00:10:16.449
Amanda?

00:10:16.449 --> 00:10:18.917
Luke, sorry, I'll call you back later, okay?

00:10:20.052 --> 00:10:22.850
I'm sorry. What were your names again?

00:10:24.123 --> 00:10:25.291
Who is it?

00:10:25.291 --> 00:10:29.022
Your friends from school. I'm going
to have them come in, okay?

00:10:30.596 --> 00:10:31.893
It should be fine.

00:10:33.466 --> 00:10:34.763
Go on in.

00:10:35.067 --> 00:10:36.068
Hello.

00:10:36.068 --> 00:10:37.035
Hello.

00:10:53.753 --> 00:10:57.156
Um, we just came to see how you are doing.

00:10:57.156 --> 00:10:59.425
Are you all right? You know, physically?

00:10:59.425 --> 00:11:02.917
Don't come here to ask me about stuff that!

00:11:04.764 --> 00:11:08.393
Just seeing your faces has
made me feel sick again.

00:11:08.768 --> 00:11:09.301
Sorry...

00:11:09.301 --> 00:11:10.069
I'm the one who asked her to come with me.
Sorry...

00:11:10.069 --> 00:11:12.094
I'm the one who asked her to come with me.

00:11:13.272 --> 00:11:14.899
You've got to be kidding me...

00:11:15.207 --> 00:11:19.234
This is a nice room. It's really pretty.

00:11:19.512 --> 00:11:22.174
I wouldn't have thought it was your style.

00:11:23.949 --> 00:11:28.409
Well, we skipped school and
started wondering, and well...

00:11:29.355 --> 00:11:31.118
You went to school?!

00:11:31.357 --> 00:11:32.124
Yeah...

00:11:32.124 --> 00:11:32.591
We skipped out early.
Yeah...

00:11:32.591 --> 00:11:33.387
We skipped out early.

00:11:35.294 --> 00:11:37.163
You're kidding?! Are you stupid?!

00:11:37.163 --> 00:11:37.596
But...

00:11:37.596 --> 00:11:38.230
I'm not joking!
But...

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:38.924
I'm not joking!

00:11:39.165 --> 00:11:42.032
School?! Skip out?!

00:11:42.702 --> 00:11:45.771
Don't you get it?! We're dead!

00:11:45.771 --> 00:11:47.796
Do you understand that?! Dead!

00:11:48.708 --> 00:11:52.109
Do the dead go to school? What about Lise?

00:11:52.311 --> 00:11:54.745
So, did Lise come today?

00:11:55.114 --> 00:11:55.815
Rachel...

00:11:55.815 --> 00:11:56.115
What were you thinking?!
Rachel...

00:11:56.115 --> 00:11:56.882
What were you thinking?!

00:11:56.882 --> 00:11:59.552
Rachel, we were just worried about you.

00:11:59.552 --> 00:12:02.817
Stop it! God, you two have some nerve!

00:12:04.457 --> 00:12:05.924
Don't make me laugh.

00:12:06.525 --> 00:12:10.359
What would make you two come to my room?

00:12:11.297 --> 00:12:13.527
You shouldn't be here.

00:12:14.033 --> 00:12:17.136
What, are we friends?

00:12:17.136 --> 00:12:21.732
Have we hung out together, Miss Grace?

00:12:25.044 --> 00:12:26.511
What should we do?

00:12:27.179 --> 00:12:31.115
Let's go. I want to talk about this with Claire too.

00:12:31.751 --> 00:12:33.048
Okay...

00:12:48.868 --> 00:12:51.170
Is that really her boyfriend?

00:12:51.170 --> 00:12:53.764
Yes, and this is our secret symbol.

00:12:56.942 --> 00:12:58.569
This is the place.

00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:11.980
Don't they know that good instincts
won't always lead to happiness?

00:13:22.234 --> 00:13:23.201
Yeah?

00:13:23.803 --> 00:13:26.505
Kate, have you ever been to
a place like this before?

00:13:26.505 --> 00:13:27.802
No!

00:13:34.146 --> 00:13:35.443
Peter!

00:13:42.655 --> 00:13:46.455
What are you doing?!
That's dangerous! Settle down!

00:13:49.395 --> 00:13:52.455
Three zero two...Three zero two...

00:13:52.665 --> 00:13:54.233
Here it is.

00:13:54.233 --> 00:13:57.760
Do you think we'll be bothering Claire too?

00:13:58.404 --> 00:14:01.669
Maybe, but we're here so...

00:14:09.014 --> 00:14:11.608
This buzzer isn't working, is it?

00:14:12.351 --> 00:14:13.875
I think it's broken.

00:14:30.669 --> 00:14:31.670
Kate...

00:14:31.670 --> 00:14:32.671
Yeah?

00:14:32.671 --> 00:14:38.837
Me...I've never had a boyfriend.
I've never traveled overseas.

00:14:39.478 --> 00:14:41.469
I haven't even been to the West Coast.

00:14:42.815 --> 00:14:50.244
When I think about, there's so much
I haven't done, so little I know.

00:14:52.524 --> 00:14:55.494
There's so many things I want to do and see.

00:14:55.494 --> 00:15:01.262
It would be so sad if everything
just ended like this.

00:15:02.501 --> 00:15:04.128
It's not over yet.

00:15:05.537 --> 00:15:07.971
It's not over...

00:15:10.109 --> 00:15:14.346
Here we are alive.

00:15:14.346 --> 00:15:17.713
I think we're different than Lise.

00:15:18.851 --> 00:15:21.945
Yeah, you're right.

00:15:22.588 --> 00:15:24.647
I'm even hungry!

00:15:25.357 --> 00:15:28.884
That's right! We can still do a lot of things!

00:15:29.028 --> 00:15:30.325
Yeah!

00:15:30.396 --> 00:15:33.132
Hey, Rose, is that good?

00:15:33.132 --> 00:15:34.429
Want to try some?

00:15:40.239 --> 00:15:41.934
It really is good!

00:15:42.341 --> 00:15:45.242
So the guy that runs that
restaurant is kind of strange.

00:15:45.377 --> 00:15:46.145
Yeah?

00:15:46.145 --> 00:15:46.946
There are these rules, and
if someone breaks them,
Yeah?

00:15:46.946 --> 00:15:47.947
There are these rules, and
if someone breaks them,

00:15:47.947 --> 00:15:51.474
he yells, "I won't sell you soup for one year!"

00:15:51.684 --> 00:15:53.552
Really? Why?

00:15:53.552 --> 00:15:57.750
Beats me. But the place is so good,
that it's always packed like that.

00:15:58.057 --> 00:16:02.494
Well, it is good, but that shop owner
sure seems like a jerk!

00:16:08.834 --> 00:16:10.233
What is it?

00:16:17.876 --> 00:16:19.173
No way...

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:22.977
Damn!

00:16:26.051 --> 00:16:28.451
You're pissing me off!

00:16:31.223 --> 00:16:33.817
Fine! I'll leave! That's what you want, right?

00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:36.389
I'll catch you one of these days!

00:16:36.729 --> 00:16:40.165
What does that girl see?

00:16:41.467 --> 00:16:44.925
Luke, I'm sorry, I just can't.

00:16:45.704 --> 00:16:48.707
I just don't feel like it.

00:16:48.707 --> 00:16:50.140
No, that's not it.

00:16:50.509 --> 00:16:51.976
Really?

00:16:52.778 --> 00:16:55.838
Rachel, somehow you've changed.

00:16:57.483 --> 00:16:59.110
No, that's not what I mean.

00:16:59.818 --> 00:17:03.422
I mean, have you become
interested in somebody else?

